 rating consensus at roughly +9.", "watch": "If Harding consolidates the district's Republican base after the debates or outside groups re-engage with spending, the race could tighten toward Lean D.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Don Bacon (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Nebraska's 2nd District is an open seat with Don Bacon retiring, and it carries a modest Democratic lean in a year when the national environment favors Democrats. Denise Powell has out-raised Brinker Harding and benefits from roughly $3.1 million in outside support, while super PACs have reportedly pulled back spending on the Republican side. A September SurveyUSA poll showed Powell up four points among likely voters.\n\nExpert raters overwhelmingly call the race a Democratic flip, ranging from Tilt D to Solid D, and prediction markets put Powell's chances around 93 percent. The race remains competitive enough that a strong Harding debate performance or renewed Republican investment could narrow the gap, but the weight of evidence points to a Likely Democratic pickup of the Omaha-area blue dot.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9278, "margin": 8.8}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9035, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.914, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9146, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8905, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9055, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.902, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8848, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9024, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9327, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9296, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9341, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.918, "margin": 8.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.882, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9087, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9075, "mar